5, 0.018360315, 0.010049976, -0.043548018, 0.02966069, 0.02698546, 0.004861084, -0.05430163, 0.011475177, 0.015738389, 0.019060077, -0.03985229, 0.030992523, -0.021415712, 0.021547105, 0.049709383, -0.019045923, 0.08639449, -0.0006299196, -0.025505854, 0.012419522, -0.05114959, -0.0133081805, -0.05731522, 0.008569001, 0.043819334, -0.007590389, -0.003940309, -0.012845572, 0.0086376425, 0.0018256578, -0.011337763, 0.050885152, 0.037154082, 0.0039129523, -0.0094618425, 0.021248708, 0.057511315, 0.028663052, 0.015481698, -0.0013716809, -0.06171668, 0.01059123, 0.043242555, 0.029275909, -0.0040734066, -0.004916001, 2.632948e-34, -0.011279975, -0.08483875, 0.027440783, 0.038380947, -0.05122291, 0.006378777, 0.02985625, -0.0032710414, -0.02289888, -0.02805654, -0.04066985], embedding_text: 'Policy: Discount Policy v2.1\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-FIN-001\n\nContent:\n# Discount Policy v2.1\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-FIN-001  \n**Version**: 2.1  \n**Effective Date**: January 15, 2024  \n**Owner**: CFO Office (Raj Patel)  \n**Last Updated**: January 15, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Quarterly  \n**Confidentiality**: Internal\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy establishes guidelines for pricing discounts on NexaTech products to ensure:\n- Consistent pricing across customer segments\n- Sustainable gross margins (target: 70%+)\n- Fair treatment of all customers\n- Clear approval workflows for exceptions\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\nThis policy applies to:\n- All NexaTech products (WorkFlow Pro, TeamSync, TalentHub)\n- New customer acquisitions\n- Renewal negotiations\n- Upsell/cross-sell transactions\n- All sales team members and executives\n\n---\n\n## 3. Standard Discount Tiers\n\n### 3.1 New Customer Discounts\n\n| Customer Tier | Annual Contract Value | Max Discount | Approval Required |\n|--------------|----------------------|--------------|-------------------|\n| SMB (1-99 employees) | ¥1M - ¥5M | 10% | AE + Sales Manager |\n| Mid-Market (100-499) | ¥5M - ¥15M | 15% | AE + Sales Director |\n| Enterprise (500-1999) | ¥15M - ¥30M | 20% | VP Sales |\n| Strategic (2000+) | ¥30M+ | 25% | VP Sales + CFO |\n\n### 3.2 Renewal Discounts\n\n| Situation | Max Discount | Approval Required |\n|-----------|--------------|-------------------|\n| On-time renewal (no churn risk) | 5% | AE |\n| At-risk customer (churn signals) | 15% | VP Sales |\n| Strategic account negotiation | 20% | VP Sales + CFO |\n| Competitive threat (documented) | 25% | VP Sales + CFO + CEO |\n\n### 3.3 Volume Discounts\n\nAutomatically applied for multi-year contracts:\n- 2-year commitment: +5% discount\n- 3-year commitment: +10% discount\n- 5-year commitment: +15% discount\n\n---\n\n## 4. Prohibited Discounts\n\nThe following are **NOT PERMITTED** without CEO approval:\n- Discounts >25% for any customer\n- Discounts applied retroactively\n- Discounts without documented business justification\n- Free product giveaways (exceptions: NFP/education sector)\n- Discounts that bring gross margin below 65%\n\n---\n\n## 5. Approval Workflow\n\n### 5.1 Standard Process\n\n1. **AE prepares discount request** with business justification including:\n   - Customer profile and strategic value\n   - Competitive landscape and pricing\n   - Expected lifetime value (LTV)\n   - Risk assessment if discount is denied\n\n2. **Required approvals** based on tier (see Section 3.1-3.2)\n\n3. **Finance review** for discounts >15%:\n   - Gross margin impact analysis\n   - CAC payback period calculation\n   - LTV:CAC ratio validation (must be >3:1)\n\n4. **Documentation** in Salesforce with:\n   - Approval chain (digital signatures)\n   - Business justification\n   - Competitive intelligence (if applicable)\n\n### 5.2 Expedited Approval (Emergency)\n\nFor time-sensitive deals requiring >20% discount:\n- VP Sales and CFO can approve jointly via Slack/email\n- Must be followed by formal documentation within 24 hours\n- Limited to 5 uses per quarter per sales team\n\n---\n\n## 6. Special Situations\n\n### 6.1 Nonprofit and Education\n\n- Eligible organizations: 30% standard discount\n- Requires verification (501(c)(3) or equivalent)\n- Annual contract minimum: ¥500K\n- Approval: VP Sales\n\n### 6.2 Strategic Partnerships\n\n- Partner/reseller discounts: 20-40% based on volume commitment\n- Requires partnership agreement\n- Approval: CEO + CFO\n\n### 6.3 Startup Programs\n\n- Early-stage startups (<50 employees, <$1M funding): 50% discount for year 1\n- Graduates to standard pricing year 2\n- Limited to 20 startups per year\n- Approval: CMO (lead generation program)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Value-Based Alternatives to Discounts\n\n**Preferred approach**: Offer value-adds instead of price reductions when possible.\n\n### 7.1 Approved Value-Adds (cost to deliver vs customer perceived value)\n\n| Value-Add | Cost to NexaTech | Customer Value | Approval |\n|-----------|-----------------|----------------|----------|\n| Dedicated CSM | ¥800K/year | ¥3M perceived | VP CS |\n| Premium support (4hr SLA) | ¥500K/year | ¥2M perceived | VP CS |\n| Custom integrations (3) | ¥1.2M one-time | ¥5M perceived | CTO |\n| Advanced analytics module | ¥300K/year | ¥2M perceived | VP Product |\n| Extended training (5 days) | ¥600K one-time | ¥1.5M perceived | VP CS |\n| Executive business reviews (quarterly) | ¥400K/year | ¥1M perceived | VP Sales |\n\n**Strategic value**: Value-adds cost less than cash discounts but have higher perceived value. Preferred for strategic accounts.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Discount Tracking and Reporting\n\n### 8.1 Monthly Reporting\n\nFinance team produces monthly discount report including:\n- Average discount by tier\n- Discount trend over time\n- Impact on gross margins\n- Top 10 discounts by dollar amount\n\n### 8.2 Quarterly Business Review\n\nCFO presents to executive team:\n- Discount policy compliance rate\n- Exception trends and patterns\n- Competitive pricing pressure analysis\n- Policy effectiveness assessment\n\n---\n\n## 9. Competitive Price Matching\n\n### 9.1 Policy\n\nNexaTech does **NOT** automatically match competitor pricing. We compete on value, not price.\n\n### 9.2 Evaluation Criteria\n\nIf customer presents competitive offer, evaluate:\n1. **Is the offer genuine?** (Request written quote)\n2. **Feature parity?** (Ensure apples-to-apples comparison)\n3. **Strategic value of customer?** (Lifetime value assessment)\n4. **Margin impact?** (Can we match and maintain 65% margin?)\n\nIf all criteria met, VP Sales + CFO can approve competitive match up to 25% discount.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Precedent Cases\n\n### 10.1 MegaCorp Japan Renewal (DC_AKIKO_001)\n\n**Situation**: Strategic customer (¥25M ARR) requested 20% renewal discount citing competitive offer.\n\n**Decision**: Approved 15% discount + ¥3M value-adds (dedicated CSM, premium features, custom integrations) structured as 3-year contract.\n\n**Rationale**: \n- Stayed within 15% policy for renewals\n- Value-adds cost ¥800K but perceived as ¥5M value\n- 3-year commitment reduced churn risk\n- Effective discount ~17% vs 20% requested\n- Protected gross margin (68% maintained)\n\n**Outcome**: Customer accepted, signed 3-year deal, later expanded by 500 seats.\n\n**Precedent**: This approach is now template for strategic account renewals >¥20M.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Policy Exceptions\n\n### 11.1 When to Request Exception\n\nSituations requiring CEO approval (outside policy boundaries):\n- Discount >25% for any reason\n- Discounts that reduce gross margin below 65%\n- Government/enterprise customers with unique requirements\n- Market entry pricing for new regions\n\n### 11.2 Exception Request Process\n\n1. VP Sales prepares detailed business case including:\n   - Why exception is necessary\n   - Long-term strategic value\n   - Financial impact analysis (3-year projection)\n   - Precedent risk assessment\n\n2. Present to CEO + CFO in joint meeting\n\n3. If approved, document rationale and set expiration date\n\n4. Exceptions reviewed quarterly to prevent policy erosion\n\n---\n\n## 12. Sales Compensation Impact\n\nSales commission is calculated on **net revenue** (after discounts):\n- Incentivizes sales team to minimize discounts\n- Higher commission % on deals with <10% discount\n- Standard commission on deals with 10-20% discount\n- Reduced commission on deals with >20% discount\n\nSee Sales Compensation Policy (POLICY-SALES-001) for details.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Policy Violations\n\n### 13.1 Consequences\n\n- **Unauthorized discount applied**: Deal subject to retrospective review, sales credit may be adjusted\n- **Repeated violations**: Performance improvement plan\n- **Intentional circumvention**: Termination\n\n### 13.2 Reporting Violations\n\nFinance team monitors all deals. Violations reported to VP Sales and CFO monthly.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Related Policies\n\n- **POLICY-SALES-001**: Sales Compensation Policy\n- **POLICY-FIN-002**: Revenue Recognition Policy  \n- **POLICY-FIN-003**: Customer Payment Terms Policy\n- **POLICY-CS-001**: Customer Contract Terms\n\n---\n\n## 15. Policy Change History\n\n| Version | Date | Changes | Approved By |\n|---------|------|---------|-------------|\n| 1.0 | 2022-06-01\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'Finance'});
