183, 0.026469178, 0.028125988, -0.016262358, -0.030323647, 0.05062301, -0.02196929, 0.017776717, -0.0726244, -0.02140575, -0.033933103, 0.03648011, 0.044734545, -0.016595945, -0.010133501, -0.0018766436, 0.031970125, 0.018050134, 0.07730338, -0.003711145, 0.029788937, 0.010812177, -0.031916253, -0.012847823, -0.053150803, -0.013016446, 0.08161127, -0.0079833055, 0.035858296, 0.024298929, 0.029037118, 0.01127636, 0.00077160617, 0.03313284, -0.004986448, -0.005083069, -0.007166004, -0.0069417395, 0.027192712, 0.033514146, 0.022020767, 0.034106113, -0.020378878, -0.02530557, 0.012981721, 0.058706295, 0.015417662, 0.012467841, 2.3558578e-34, -0.013533716, -0.072791524, -0.027064092, -0.00825518, -0.019797854, -0.026647096, 0.005110787, 0.017203668, -0.0045965463, -0.039041992, -0.0140418615], embedding_text: 'Policy: Travel Expense Policy\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-FIN-004\n\nContent:\n# Travel Expense Policy\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-FIN-004  \n**Version**: 1.3  \n**Effective Date**: March 1, 2024  \n**Owner**: CFO Office (Raj Patel)  \n**Last Updated**: March 1, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Annually  \n**Confidentiality**: Internal\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy establishes guidelines for business travel expenses to ensure:\n- Cost-effective travel arrangements\n- Consistent expense standards across organization\n- Timely reimbursement for employees\n- Compliance with tax regulations\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\nApplies to all NexaTech employees traveling for business purposes including:\n- Customer meetings and conferences\n- Sales calls and prospecting\n- Partner meetings\n- Company offsites and events\n- Training and professional development\n\n---\n\n## 3. Travel Approval\n\n### 3.1 Domestic Travel (within Japan)\n\n| Purpose | Approval Required |\n|---------|------------------|\n| Customer meetings | Manager approval |\n| Conferences (registration <¥50K) | Manager approval |\n| Conferences (registration ≥¥50K) | Department head approval |\n| Team offsites | Department head approval |\n\n### 3.2 International Travel\n\n| Purpose | Approval Required |\n|---------|------------------|\n| Customer meetings | VP + CFO approval |\n| Conferences | VP + CFO approval |\n| Sales prospects | VP Sales + CFO approval |\n| Executive travel | CEO approval |\n\n**Advance notice**: International travel requires 14 days advance approval except emergencies.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Transportation\n\n### 4.1 Air Travel\n\n**Class of Service**:\n- **Domestic flights**: Economy class\n- **International flights <6 hours**: Economy class\n- **International flights ≥6 hours**: Premium economy (VP and above) or Economy (all others)\n- **International flights ≥12 hours**: Business class (C-level only)\n\n**Booking**:\n- Book at least 14 days in advance when possible\n- Use approved travel agency or company booking tool\n- Choose lowest logical airfare considering:\n  - Schedule efficiency\n  - Connection times\n  - Total travel time\n\n**Exceptions**: \n- Medical conditions requiring upgrade: Manager + HR approval\n- Emergency travel: VP approval\n\n### 4.2 Rail Travel (Shinkansen, etc.)\n\n- **Green Car**: Allowed for travel >2 hours\n- **Ordinary Car**: Standard for travel <2 hours\n- Book Reserved seats when available\n\n### 4.3 Ground Transportation\n\n**Taxis/Ride-sharing**:\n- Allowed when public transportation is impractical\n- Required receipts for all rides\n- Pool with colleagues when possible\n\n**Rental Cars**:\n- Economy or compact class\n- Requires manager pre-approval\n- Include insurance coverage\n- Gas receipts required\n\n**Personal Vehicle**:\n- Reimbursement: ¥20/km\n- Parking receipts required\n- Insurance coverage confirmation required\n\n---\n\n## 5. Accommodations\n\n### 5.1 Hotel Standards\n\n| Employee Level | Max Per Night (¥) - Tokyo/Major Cities | Max Per Night (¥) - Other Cities |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| Individual Contributor | 18,000 | 12,000 |\n| Manager | 22,000 | 15,000 |\n| Director/VP | 28,000 | 20,000 |\n| C-Level | 35,000 | 25,000 |\n\n**Guidelines**:\n- Book hotels within reasonable distance of meeting location\n- Use corporate-rate hotels when available\n- Extended stays (>5 nights): Negotiate weekly rate\n\n**Exceptions**:\n- Conference hotel (if conference venue): Allowed at conference rate\n- Peak season/limited availability: VP approval for exceeding limits\n\n---\n\n## 6. Meals and Entertainment\n\n### 6.1 Meals (Per Diem)\n\nWhen traveling, per diem allowance (no receipts required under limit):\n\n| Meal | Domestic (¥) | International (¥) |\n|------|--------------|------------------|\n| Breakfast | 1,500 | 2,000 |\n| Lunch | 2,000 | 2,500 |\n| Dinner | 3,500 | 5,000 |\n| **Daily Total** | **7,000** | **9,500** |\n\n**Notes**:\n- If hotel includes breakfast, deduct ¥1,500 from per diem\n- Receipts required for meals exceeding per diem\n- Alcohol: Max ¥3,000/day included in dinner allowance\n\n### 6.2 Client Entertainment\n\n**Limits**:\n- Sales meals with prospects: ¥15,000 per person\n- Executive client dinners: ¥25,000 per person\n- Client entertainment (events, activities): Requires VP approval\n\n**Requirements**:\n- Receipt required\n- Document attendees and business purpose\n- No entertainment without business discussion\n\n---\n\n## 7. Conference and Event Expenses\n\n### 7.1 Conference Registration\n\n**Approval Limits**:\n- <¥50,000: Manager approval\n- ¥50,000 - ¥150,000: Department head approval\n- >¥150,000: VP + CFO approval\n\n**Early bird discounts**: Book early when available (typically 20-30% savings)\n\n### 7.2 Conference Travel\n\nWhen attending conferences:\n- Hotel: Conference hotel rate allowed (even if exceeds policy limits)\n- Meals: Per diem + reasonable conference meals\n- Networking events: Included in conference purpose\n\n---\n\n## 8. Expense Reporting\n\n### 8.1 Submission Timeline\n\n- Submit expense reports within **14 days** of trip completion\n- Monthly travelers: Submit by 5th of following month\n- Reimbursement: Within 15 business days of approval\n\n### 8.2 Required Documentation\n\nFor each expense:\n- ☐ Original itemized receipt (photo acceptable)\n- ☐ Business purpose description\n- ☐ Attendees (for meals/entertainment)\n- ☐ Mileage log (for personal vehicle)\n- ☐ Foreign currency exchange rate (for international)\n\n### 8.3 Expense Categories\n\nUse correct categories in expense system:\n- **TRAVEL-AIR**: Airfare\n- **TRAVEL-RAIL**: Train/Shinkansen\n- **TRAVEL-GROUND**: Taxi, rental car, parking\n- **TRAVEL-HOTEL**: Lodging\n- **TRAVEL-MEALS**: Meals (per diem or actual)\n- **TRAVEL-CONFERENCE**: Registration fees\n- **TRAVEL-CLIENT**: Client entertainment\n- **TRAVEL-OTHER**: Misc (internet, baggage fees, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## 9. Prohibited Expenses\n\nThe following are **NOT reimbursable**:\n- ❌ Personal travel expenses\n- ❌ Spouse/family travel (unless approved by CEO)\n- ❌ In-room entertainment (movies, minibar)\n- ❌ Personal grooming (haircuts, spa)\n- ❌ Traffic violations or parking fines\n- ❌ Lost baggage or personal items\n- ❌ Travel insurance (company policy covers business travel)\n- ❌ Commuting to/from regular office\n\n---\n\n## 10. International Travel Considerations\n\n### 10.1 Currency Exchange\n\n- Use corporate credit card for charges (best exchange rate)\n- If using personal funds, reimburse at rate on transaction date\n- Attach screenshot of exchange rate from xe.com or equivalent\n\n### 10.2 Visas and Vaccinations\n\n- Visa fees: Reimbursable for business travel\n- Required vaccinations: Reimbursable with medical receipt\n- Passport fees: Not reimbursable (personal document)\n\n### 10.3 Travel Insurance\n\n- Company policy covers international business travel\n- Submit claims to HR for medical issues abroad\n- Travel delay/cancellation covered by corporate credit card\n\n---\n\n## 11. Corporate Credit Cards\n\n### 11.1 Eligibility\n\nCorporate cards issued to:\n- All employees who travel monthly\n- Directors and above (regardless of travel frequency)\n- Others by exception (CFO approval)\n\n### 11.2 Usage\n\n**Authorized**:\n- Business travel expenses\n- Client entertainment (within policy)\n- Business supplies/equipment\n- Conference registrations\n\n**Prohibited**:\n- Personal purchases\n- Cash advances\n- Lending to colleagues\n- Purchases for non-employees\n\n### 11.3 Reconciliation\n\n- Review and approve charges within 5 business days\n- Attach receipts for all charges >¥5,000\n- Dispute charges immediately with provider\n\n---\n\n## 12. Frequent Flyer and Hotel Points\n\n- **Ownership**: Points earned on business travel belong to employee\n- **Usage**: May use for personal travel\n- **Upgrades**: May use points to upgrade business class (at your discretion)\n\n**Company benefits**:\n- Use corporate membership numbers when available\n- Negotiated corporate rates benefit company\n\n---\n\n## 13. Travel Advances\n\n### 13.1 Eligibility\n\nTravel advances available for:\n- International travel >¥100,000 estimated expenses\n- Extended travel (>7 days)\n- Employees without corporate credit card\n\n### 13.2 Process\n\n1. Request advance 10 days before travel via expense syst\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'Finance'});
CREATE (n34:Policy {file_path: 'test_data/policies/remote_work_policy.md', last_updated: neo4j.time.Date(2024, 1, 1), confidentiality: 'Internal', embedding_model: 'sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2', owner_executive: 'Akiko Tanaka', review_frequency: 'Annually', version: '1.3', embedding_date: neo4j.time.DateTime(2025, 10, 24, 4, 45, 3, 183000000, tzinfo=<UTC>), embedding_dimensions: 768, name: 'Remote Work Policy', effective_date: neo4j.time.Date(2024, 1, 1), id: 'POLICY-HR-001', embedding: [0.028952638, 0.011009202, -0.042681552, -0.057939656, 0.017700123, 0.0070401044, 0.06949417, 0.08568361, -0.08611789, 0.0024106132, -0.012715825, 0.013627315, 0.007435328, 0.07856535, 0.027115889, -0.015236868, -0.021182744, 0.03739378, -0.026461743, 0.0020191069, -0.023963256, -0.020511722, -0.021623697, 0.017749324, -0.0037289623, 0.015121217, 0.038942795, 0.0028374775, 0.021323256, 0.052139916, 0.08454852, -0.02226756, -0.010618742, -0.017164942, 2.1311212e-06, -0.004266855, -0.00811666, 0.025015341, 0.021942124, -0.019205967, -0.013278995, -0.06151265, -0.025935823, 0.04711281, -0.0017370102, -0.002295466, -0.019949544, -0.023368066, 0.030546084, 0.0392792, -0.045243584, 0.018221943, -0.113924846, 0.0022387702, -0.03104299, 0.047079507, -0.0017147141, -0.056643844, -0.029736074, -0.023228843, 0.041665122, -0.043562833, 0.031097585, 0.013474919, -0.009268084, 0.03855515, -0.002885826, -0.053400774, 0.04718381, 0.010199198, 0.0365729, 0.047493324, 0.0011615834, 0.009391798, -0.005115582, -0.008522694, 0.015980897, 0.020939004, -0.008441155, -0.05626775, 0.018981073, 0.07299441, -0.04975855, -0.06574214, 0.012638395, 0.06693677, 0.0032790091, -0.013227189, -0.033119973, -0.024188602, 0.041138534, 0.009987017, 0.0029518714, 0.035007942, 0.011293266, 0.0009990585, 0.026661806, -0.011147908, 0.021887608, -0.007146969, -0.020696223, 0.005922673, 0.012588272, 0.00864779, 0.049299527, -0.012953901, -0.0078230435, -0.025172267, -0.00028794695, -0.012711974, 0.036178827, 0.0034