03, 0.0118440585, 0.019606968, -0.038934715, -0.009184331, -0.057342693, -0.009955484, 0.033479635, 0.025311936, 0.0107160555, -0.046454076, 0.045758367, -0.0013416844, -0.01047319, 0.0008035826, -0.029920079, -0.04717677, 0.0021783279, 0.02419105, 0.008568436, -1.0673684e-05, -0.0041821664, 0.0024844734, 0.050408654, 0.0046120225, 0.022632096, 0.014401007, -0.02255823, -0.011329632, -0.07101646, -0.0077759903, 0.06474727, -0.08314838, -0.030625002, -0.061129544, 0.008335797, -0.014425829, -0.013716766, -0.0007384365, 0.026573202, 0.0132816145, -0.01961322, 0.019538347, -0.03853181, -0.08267586, 0.064631306, -0.031388894, -0.022983372, -0.028786827, 0.090404466, -0.011721357, -0.020517576, -0.010050739, -0.08599822, -0.06930585, 0.008585505, -0.022814862, -0.0019177403, -0.02519692, -0.037438802, 0.037116423, -0.02427067, 0.021067139, 0.029323244, -0.03316851, -0.019943114, -0.005393254, -0.006516176, -0.039936427, 0.04267299, -0.004539038, -0.02719461, -0.021471862, 0.020451043, -0.007846468, 0.046989158, 0.05659954, -0.0030812072, 0.0154131465, -0.016076319, 0.051579345, -0.054617114, -0.03120122, -0.037709292, 0.02862809, 0.044259813, 0.02036777, -0.0015636948, -0.0130590005, -0.024377195, 0.047588527, 0.05527239, 0.06485787, -0.020032804, 0.0055996072, -0.06915827, -0.036099114, -0.022214785, -0.058089368, 0.05782587, 0.004120384, 0.002107071, 0.0018858684, 0.0063728923, 0.0024504832, 0.018470762, 0.02054508, -0.016205596, 0.022232866, -0.005968392, -0.015755195, -0.014472409, 0.049121995, 0.0392891, 0.062571004, -0.013389788, 0.020556543, 0.009545175, 0.01786901, -0.010918303, -0.01286954, 0.032282483, -0.018330457, 0.042531703, 0.018452013, 0.012943964, 0.016302206, -0.03588579, 2.8285044e-07, 0.02078674, -0.049267355, -0.055994466, 0.045898158, 0.041885376, -0.04448749, -0.0030856621, -0.04198876, 0.042475674, 0.06551376, 0.062127236, -0.045322612, 0.03357224, -0.017772034, -0.035512716, -0.05343964, 0.018137328, -0.015968055, -0.03199035, 0.045638256, 0.10517188, 0.029726692, 0.017180001, -0.0067492155, 0.028758135, -0.012975657, 0.0010324101, 0.024039984, 0.005276606, -0.019901354, 0.01426192, -0.026271824, 0.0069916537, -0.024283182, 0.007528945, 0.018679028, 0.040182903, 0.10595148, -0.03363115, 0.011860135, 0.03513033, -0.049334668, 0.008367819, -0.033974554, -0.02260553, -0.015431172, -0.015404983, 0.07883827, -0.015417209, -0.03225506, 0.018415619, -0.0017876233, 0.01749647, -0.01713435, 0.01895004, -0.04091209, -0.034231696, 0.052584916, 0.043696303, 0.043857083, -0.0053525725, -0.06797175, -0.007267542, 0.020197494, 0.0641096, 0.069028534, 0.007664894, 2.300473e-34, -0.061398424, 0.00263735, -0.0544312, 0.026845127, -0.0341781, -0.0107865995, 0.0032421893, 0.007361866, 0.012910298, -0.02775102, -0.022480158], embedding_text: 'Policy: Remote Work Policy\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-HR-001\n\nContent:\n# Remote Work Policy\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-HR-001  \n**Version**: 2.0  \n**Effective Date**: April 1, 2024  \n**Owner**: People Operations  \n**Last Updated**: April 1, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Annually  \n**Confidentiality**: Internal\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy defines NexaTech\'s approach to remote and flexible work to:\n- Enable work-life balance and employee well-being\n- Maintain productivity and collaboration\n- Support diverse working styles\n- Comply with labor regulations\n\n---\n\n## 2. Philosophy\n\nNexaTech believes in **"work from anywhere within Japan"** with the following principles:\n- **Flexibility first**: Trust employees to work where they\'re most effective\n- **Results matter**: Focus on outcomes, not hours or location\n- **Collaboration required**: Balance individual flexibility with team needs\n- **Equal treatment**: Remote employees have same opportunities as office-based\n\n---\n\n## 3. Eligibility\n\n### 3.1 Eligible Roles\n\n**Fully Remote Eligible**:\n- Engineering (all roles)\n- Product (Product Managers, Designers)\n- Marketing (Content, Digital Marketing, Analytics)\n- Customer Success (CSMs, Support)\n- Finance (FP&A, Accounting)\n\n**Hybrid Eligible** (2-3 days office per week):\n- Sales (needs customer meeting flexibility)\n- Executive team (strategic collaboration)\n- People Operations (employee support)\n\n**Office-Based**:\n- Reception/Office Operations\n- IT Support (on-site requirements)\n\n### 3.2 Employee Requirements\n\nTo be eligible for full remote work:\n- ✓ Completed 3-month probation period\n- ✓ Performance rating "Meets Expectations" or higher\n- ✓ Role eligible per Section 3.1\n- ✓ Manager approval\n- ✓ Appropriate home workspace (Section 6)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Work Arrangements\n\n### 4.1 Full-Time Remote\n\n- Work from home or other location within Japan\n- Required to visit Tokyo office once per month (travel reimbursed)\n- Must attend quarterly team gatherings (travel + accommodation reimbursed)\n- Core hours: 10:00-15:00 JST (available for meetings)\n\n### 4.2 Hybrid\n\n- Minimum 2 days/week in office (team decides which days)\n- Flexible which days based on meetings/collaboration needs\n- Core hours: 10:00-16:00 on office days\n\n### 4.3 Office-Based with Flexibility\n\n- Primary work location: Tokyo office\n- Can work remotely 1 day/week with manager approval\n- Flexible start times (7:00-10:00 arrival)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Work Hours and Availability\n\n### 5.1 Core Hours\n\nAll employees must be available during **core hours**:\n- **Core hours**: 10:00-15:00 JST (5 hours)\n- Respond to Slack/email within 2 hours during core hours\n- Attend scheduled meetings during core hours\n\n### 5.2 Flexible Hours\n\nOutside core hours, employees may:\n- Start early (7:00-10:00) or finish late (after 19:00)\n- Take breaks for personal needs (childcare, appointments)\n- Adjust schedule for optimal productivity\n\n**Total work expectation**: 8 hours/day, 40 hours/week\n\n### 5.3 Overtime\n\nRemote employees eligible for overtime pay same as office employees:\n- Overtime requires manager pre-approval\n- Tracked via time-tracking system\n- Compensated per labor law\n\n---\n\n## 6. Home Workspace Requirements\n\n### 6.1 Minimum Standards\n\nRemote employees must have:\n- ☐ Dedicated workspace (separate from personal areas)\n- ☐ Ergonomic desk and chair\n- ☐ Reliable high-speed internet (≥50 Mbps)\n- ☐ Quiet environment for calls/meetings\n- ☐ Appropriate lighting\n\n### 6.2 Company-Provided Equipment\n\nNexaTech provides:\n- Laptop (MacBook Pro or equivalent)\n- External monitor (24" or 27")\n- Keyboard and mouse\n- Headset with microphone\n- Laptop stand\n- Webcam (if needed)\n\n### 6.3 Home Office Stipend\n\n**One-time setup**: ¥100,000 for:\n- Desk and ergonomic chair\n- Lighting\n- Office supplies\n\n**Monthly stipend**: ¥5,000 for:\n- Internet costs\n- Electricity\n- Phone/mobile data\n\nSubmit expenses via expense system with receipts.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Communication and Collaboration\n\n### 7.1 Required Tools\n\n- **Slack**: Primary communication (check every 2 hours during core hours)\n- **Zoom**: Video meetings (camera ON for team meetings)\n- **WorkFlow Pro**: Project management and collaboration\n- **Email**: External communication and formal notices\n\n### 7.2 Meeting Etiquette\n\n**For all remote participants**:\n- ✓ Camera ON for team meetings (unless bandwidth issues)\n- ✓ Mute when not speaking\n- ✓ Use virtual backgrounds if home environment distracting\n- ✓ Be on time (within 2 minutes)\n\n**For meeting organizers**:\n- ✓ Record meetings for those who can\'t attend\n- ✓ Share notes and action items post-meeting\n- ✓ Schedule during core hours when possible\n\n### 7.3 Response Time Expectations\n\n| Channel | Expected Response Time |\n|---------|----------------------|\n| Slack (urgent) | 30 minutes during core hours |\n| Slack (normal) | 2 hours during core hours |\n| Email | 24 hours (business days) |\n| Phone call | Immediate (if available) |\n\n**Status indicators**:\n- 🟢 Available: Respond within 30 min\n- 🟡 Busy: Respond within 2 hours\n- 🔴 Do Not Disturb: Emergency only\n- ⚫ Away: Not available (use calendar)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Performance and Productivity\n\n### 8.1 Performance Standards\n\nRemote employees held to **same performance standards** as office employees:\n- Evaluated on outcomes and deliverables\n- Regular 1:1s with manager (weekly or bi-weekly)\n- Quarterly performance reviews\n- Annual goal setting\n\n### 8.2 Productivity Monitoring\n\nNexaTech does **NOT** use:\n- ❌ Surveillance software\n- ❌ Keystroke monitoring\n- ❌ Screenshot tools\n- ❌ Activity trackers\n\nWe **DO** use:\n- ✓ Project deliverables and milestones\n- ✓ Meeting attendance\n- ✓ Code commits (engineers)\n- ✓ Self-reported time (for compliance)\n\n**Trust-based model**: We hire adults and treat them as such.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Security and Data Protection\n\n### 9.1 Data Security Requirements\n\nRemote employees must:\n- ☐ Use company VPN when accessing internal systems\n- ☐ Enable full-disk encryption on company devices\n- ☐ Use strong passwords + 2FA for all accounts\n- ☐ Lock computer when stepping away\n- ☐ Never share login credentials\n- ☐ Report security incidents immediately\n\n### 9.2 Prohibited Actions\n\n- ❌ Working in public places (cafes, co-working) when handling sensitive data\n- ❌ Using public WiFi without VPN\n- ❌ Allowing family/friends to use company devices\n- ❌ Storing company data on personal devices\n- ❌ Discussing confidential matters in public\n\nSee Information Security Policy (POLICY-IT-001) for full requirements.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Remote Work from Abroad (Temporary)\n\n### 10.1 Short-Term (≤14 days)\n\nEmployees may work remotely from abroad for ≤14 days with:\n- Manager approval (5 days advance notice)\n- Stable internet and workspace\n- Consideration of time zone differences\n\n**Not considered**: Business travel or vacation (separate policies apply)\n\n### 10.2 Extended (15-90 days)\n\nRequires additional approvals:\n- Manager + HR + Legal approval\n- 30 days advance notice\n- Tax implications review\n- Labor law compliance check\n- Time zone compatibility plan\n\n**Limitations**:\n- Must work ≥4 hours overlap with Tokyo core hours\n- Limited to 90 days per year total\n- Not available during probation period\n\n### 10.3 Permanent Relocation Abroad\n\nNot permitted under current policy. Requires:\n- Case-by-case approval from CEO\n- Legal entity in target country or EOR arrangement\n- Salary adjustment to local market\n\n---\n\n## 11. Team Gatherings and Office Visits\n\n### 11.1 Quarterly Team Offsites\n\nAll remote employees required to attend:\n- Frequency: Once per quarter (4x per year)\n- Duration: 2-3 days\n- Location: Tokyo or regional office\n- Company covers: Travel, hotel, meals\n\n**Purpose**: Team bonding, strategic planning, face-to-face collaboration\n\n### 11.2 Monthly Office Visits\n\nFull-time remote employees expected to visit Tokyo office:\n- Frequency: Once per month minimum\n- Duration: 1-2 days\n- Company covers: Travel (if outside Tokyo area)\n\n**Purpose**: Maintain connection, casual collaboration, use office resources\n\n### 11.3 Optional Office Time\n\nOffice always available for remote employees:\n- Book desk via office management system\n- U\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'People'});
CREATE (n35:Company {arr: 3200000.0, size: 'Mid-Market', customer_since: '2023-09-14', name: 'EduTech Japan', description: 'Education technology platform', industry: 'Education', id: 'company_edutech', type: 'customer', region: 'Japan', relationship: 'Active Customer'});
