6241466, 0.03817179, 0.033915695, -0.047492612, 0.047768947, 0.034950234, 0.014281943, -0.049638588, 0.021508103, -0.03521645, 0.039027005, 0.051854372, 0.03520511, -0.0035917147, -0.0074318615, 0.02111631, 0.009246088, 0.08927045, 0.0038655852, 0.029587887, 0.04085183, -0.054445516, -0.015535431, -0.050724067, 0.045257673, 0.049649622, -0.039280258, 0.033505034, 0.014580182, -0.029802036, 0.027393963, -0.020183088, -0.0028053133, -0.010232697, 0.013020534, -0.023810754, 0.0128256185, 0.024436947, 0.041985456, 0.015346658, 0.030466024, -0.05462865, 0.00028926186, 0.019148102, 0.065489605, 0.016381364, 0.05474496, 2.6549197e-34, -0.02977284, -0.064888835, -0.031494785, -0.00083407224, -0.024178881, -0.02590018, 0.07584796, 0.035121046, 0.00011512117, -0.024541855, -0.017406976], embedding_text: 'Policy: Data Privacy Policy\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-IT-003\n\nContent:\n# Data Privacy Policy\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-IT-003  \n**Version**: 2.2  \n**Effective Date**: May 1, 2024  \n**Owner**: CTO Office (Yuki Nakamura) + Legal  \n**Last Updated**: May 1, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Annually  \n**Confidentiality**: Public (Customer-Facing Version Available)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy defines how NexaTech collects, uses, stores, and protects personal data to:\n- Comply with Japan Privacy Law (APPI) and GDPR\n- Protect customer and employee privacy\n- Build trust through transparency\n- Enable data subject rights\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\nThis policy applies to:\n- Customer personal data (primary focus)\n- Employee personal data\n- Prospect and lead data\n- Vendor and partner data\n\n**Geographic scope**: Japan (primary), EU (GDPR), Global\n\n---\n\n## 3. Legal Framework\n\n### 3.1 Applicable Laws\n\n**Japan**:\n- Act on the Protection of Personal Information (APPI) - 2022 Amendment\n- Telecommunications Business Act\n\n**European Union**:\n- General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) - for EU customers\n\n**Industry Standards**:\n- SOC 2 Type II compliance\n- ISO 27001 (target certification 2025)\n\n### 3.2 Data Protection Officer\n\n**Role**: Oversees privacy compliance, handles data subject requests\n\n**Contact**:\n- **Name**: Legal Counsel (acting DPO)\n- **Email**: privacy@nexatech.jp\n- **Phone**: +81-3-XXXX-XXXX\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data We Collect\n\n### 4.1 Customer Data\n\n**Account Information**:\n- Name (individual and company)\n- Email address\n- Phone number\n- Company name and size\n- Billing address\n- Payment information (tokenized)\n\n**Usage Data**:\n- Login timestamps\n- Feature usage\n- IP addresses\n- Browser and device information\n- Performance metrics\n\n**Content Data** (customer-created):\n- Projects, tasks, files uploaded by customer\n- Comments and collaboration data\n- Customer-generated reports\n\n**Support Data**:\n- Support tickets and correspondence\n- Chat logs with support team\n- Product feedback\n\n### 4.2 Employee Data\n\n- Name, address, contact information\n- Employment history and qualifications\n- Performance reviews\n- Compensation and benefits\n- Time and attendance\n- Emergency contacts\n\n### 4.3 Marketing Data\n\n- Website visitors (cookies, analytics)\n- Form submissions (downloads, demo requests)\n- Email engagement (opens, clicks)\n- Event attendance\n\n---\n\n## 5. Legal Basis for Processing\n\n### 5.1 For Customer Data\n\n**Contractual necessity**:\n- Providing services customer purchased\n- Billing and payments\n- Customer support\n\n**Legitimate interests**:\n- Improving product quality\n- Security and fraud prevention\n- Analytics and optimization\n\n**Consent**:\n- Marketing communications (opt-in required)\n- Cookies (non-essential)\n- Product research participation\n\n**Legal obligation**:\n- Tax and accounting records\n- Responding to legal requests\n\n### 5.2 For Employee Data\n\n**Employment contract**:\n- Payroll and benefits administration\n- Performance management\n- Workplace safety\n\n**Legal obligation**:\n- Tax withholding\n- Social insurance\n- Labor law compliance\n\n---\n\n## 6. How We Use Data\n\n### 6.1 Primary Purposes\n\n**Service delivery**:\n- Provide access to products\n- Process transactions\n- Deliver customer support\n- Send service notifications\n\n**Product improvement**:\n- Analyze usage patterns\n- Identify bugs and issues\n- Develop new features\n- Optimize performance\n\n**Business operations**:\n- Financial reporting\n- Legal compliance\n- Internal analytics\n\n**Security**:\n- Fraud prevention\n- Abuse detection\n- Access control\n- Incident response\n\n### 6.2 Marketing (Opt-In Only)\n\n**With customer consent**:\n- Product updates and newsletters\n- Event invitations\n- Educational content\n- Feature announcements\n\n**Opt-out**: Every marketing email includes unsubscribe link. Opt-out honored within 48 hours.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Data Sharing and Disclosure\n\n### 7.1 We DO NOT Sell Data\n\nNexaTech **never sells** customer data to third parties.\n\n### 7.2 Sharing with Service Providers\n\nWe share data with trusted vendors for:\n\n**Infrastructure providers**:\n- AWS (cloud hosting) - USA\n- Google Cloud (backup) - Japan region\n- Cloudflare (CDN) - Global\n\n**Business tools**:\n- Intercom (customer support) - USA\n- Stripe (payment processing) - USA\n- SendGrid (transactional email) - USA\n- Mixpanel (product analytics) - USA\n\n**Requirements for vendors**:\n- Data Processing Agreement (DPA) signed\n- GDPR-compliant (for EU data)\n- SOC 2 certified or equivalent\n- Data only used for specified purpose\n- Security standards verified\n\n### 7.3 Legal Disclosures\n\nWe may disclose data when:\n- Required by law (court order, subpoena)\n- Protecting rights, property, or safety\n- Business transaction (merger, acquisition)\n- With customer consent\n\n**Transparency commitment**: We notify customers of legal requests unless prohibited by law.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Data Storage and Security\n\n### 8.1 Storage Locations\n\n**Primary data center**: AWS Tokyo region (ap-northeast-1)  \n**Backup data center**: AWS Osaka region (ap-northeast-3)  \n**Data residency**: Customer data stays in Japan unless customer consents to international transfer\n\n**For EU customers**:\n- Data stored in AWS Frankfurt (eu-central-1) or customer\'s chosen EU region\n- Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) for any transfers\n\n### 8.2 Security Measures\n\n**Technical controls** (see Information Security Policy for details):\n- Encryption at rest (AES-256)\n- Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+)\n- Multi-factor authentication\n- Access controls and least privilege\n- Regular security testing\n- Intrusion detection\n- Backup and disaster recovery\n\n**Organizational controls**:\n- Security training for all staff\n- Background checks for employees\n- Confidentiality agreements\n- Incident response procedures\n- Regular security audits\n\n### 8.3 Data Breach Response\n\n**If breach occurs**:\n1. Contain breach immediately (<2 hours)\n2. Assess impact (what data, how many affected)\n3. Notify regulators within 72 hours (APPI/GDPR requirement)\n4. Notify affected individuals without undue delay\n5. Public disclosure if material\n6. Offer remediation (identity monitoring if appropriate)\n\n**See**: Security Incident DC_YUKI_005 for precedent of transparent breach response.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Data Retention\n\n### 9.1 Customer Data\n\n**Active customers**:\n- Account data: Duration of subscription\n- Usage data: 90 days (rolling)\n- Content data: Duration of subscription + 30 days after cancellation\n- Support data: 2 years\n\n**Inactive customers** (post-cancellation):\n- Account data: 30 days (then deleted)\n- Content data: 30 days (then deleted unless legal hold)\n- Billing data: 7 years (tax/legal requirement)\n\n**Marketing data**:\n- Opted-in contacts: Until opt-out + 30 days\n- Opted-out contacts: Suppression list (permanent, to honor opt-out)\n\n### 9.2 Employee Data\n\n**Current employees**:\n- All employment data retained\n\n**Former employees**:\n- Personnel file: 7 years after termination\n- Payroll records: 7 years (tax requirement)\n- Performance reviews: 3 years\n- Other data: Deleted within 1 year unless legal hold\n\n### 9.3 Backups\n\n**Backup retention**:\n- Daily backups: 30 days\n- Weekly backups: 90 days\n- Quarterly backups: 1 year\n\n**Backup deletion**: Overwritten after retention period, not individually deletable (technical limitation).\n\n**Legal holds**: If data subject to litigation/investigation, retained until hold lifted.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Data Subject Rights\n\n### 10.1 Your Rights (APPI & GDPR)\n\n**Right to access**: Request copy of your personal data\n\n**Right to rectification**: Correct inaccurate data\n\n**Right to erasure** ("right to be forgotten"): Delete data when no longer necessary\n\n**Right to restriction**: Limit how we use data\n\n**Right to portability**: Receive data in machine-readable format\n\n**Right to object**: Object to certain processing (e.g., marketing)\n\n**Right to withdraw consent**: For consent-based processing\n\n**Right to complain**: Lodge complaint with supervisory authority\n\n### 10.2 How to Exercise Rights\n\n**Submit request**:\n- **Email**: privacy@nexatech.jp\n- **Web form**: https://nexatech.jp/privacy-request\n- **Mail**: Ne\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'IT'});
