33235, 0.017277237, -0.009441771, 0.06513994, -0.035829622, 0.055427905, 0.08003195, -0.008323136, -0.063705675, -0.03643379, 0.027871354, -0.029296318, -0.030194588, 0.004953576, 0.013622476, -0.008632476, 0.03334554, 0.027357694, 0.038414247, -0.010565538, -0.0065586, 0.010188958, -0.018697249, -0.005597983, -0.043013524, -0.023269717, 0.016571453, -0.08061142, -0.03453596, 0.021741463, 0.0052961023, -0.010689202, 0.016702402, 0.028140156, -0.009199496, 0.0011583072, 0.022376878, -0.0005590564, 0.044240043, 0.00037981535, 0.040633954, -0.01601214, -0.03489078, 0.018501831, 0.028535612, 0.011142587, -0.06260636, -0.0023121506, 2.1513257e-34, -0.03550702, -0.054953326, -0.015983192, 0.00044730827, -0.025862755, -0.0063776816, 0.03738512, 0.005358648, 0.01618922, 0.025294619, -0.052602194], embedding_text: 'Policy: Sales Compensation Policy\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-SALES-001\n\nContent:\n# Sales Compensation Policy\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-SALES-001  \n**Version**: 2.3  \n**Effective Date**: January 1, 2024  \n**Owner**: VP Sales (Kenji Sato) + CFO (Raj Patel)  \n**Last Updated**: January 1, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Annually  \n**Confidentiality**: Internal - Sales Team Only\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy establishes sales compensation structure to:\n- Align sales incentives with company revenue goals\n- Reward high performance\n- Promote sustainable customer acquisition\n- Balance new business and renewals\n- Ensure fair and transparent compensation\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\nApplies to:\n- Account Executives (AEs)\n- Sales Development Representatives (SDRs)\n- Account Managers (AMs)\n- Sales management (VP Sales, Sales Directors)\n\nDoes NOT apply to:\n- Customer Success (separate compensation plan)\n- Pre-sales engineers (bonus based on company performance)\n- Marketing (separate bonus structure)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Compensation Structure\n\n### 3.1 OTE (On-Target Earnings)\n\n**OTE = Base Salary + Target Commission**\n\nAssumes 100% quota attainment\n\n| Role | Base Salary | Target Commission | OTE | Variable % |\n|------|-------------|-------------------|-----|------------|\n| SDR | ¥4,500K | ¥1,500K | ¥6,000K | 25% |\n| AE (Mid-Market) | ¥7,000K | ¥5,000K | ¥12,000K | 42% |\n| AE (Enterprise) | ¥8,000K | ¥7,000K | ¥15,000K | 47% |\n| Account Manager | ¥6,500K | ¥3,500K | ¥10,000K | 35% |\n| Sales Director | ¥10,000K | ¥4,000K | ¥14,000K | 29% |\n| VP Sales | ¥13,000K | ¥5,000K | ¥18,000K | 28% |\n\n**Philosophy**: Higher variable % for individual contributors, lower for management\n\n### 3.2 Base Salary\n\n**Paid**: Monthly (12 equal installments)\n\n**Adjustments**: Annual review based on performance and market\n\n**Guaranteed**: Base salary is guaranteed regardless of sales performance\n\n### 3.3 Commission\n\n**Earned**: Based on closed deals and quota attainment\n\n**Paid**: Monthly (for deals closed in previous month)\n\n**Clawback**: See Section 8 for clawback conditions\n\n---\n\n## 4. Quota Setting\n\n### 4.1 Quota Assignment\n\n**Annual quotas** set by:\n- Company revenue target\n- Territory/segment allocation\n- Historical performance\n- Market opportunity\n- Ramp time (for new hires)\n\n**Example**: If company target is ¥4.5B revenue, and we have 10 AEs, average quota is ¥450M per AE (adjusted by territory)\n\n### 4.2 Quota by Role\n\n| Role | Annual Quota | Quota Type |\n|------|--------------|------------|\n| SDR | 120 SRLs (Sales-Ready Leads) | Activity-based |\n| AE (Mid-Market) | ¥60M ARR | Revenue-based |\n| AE (Enterprise) | ¥80M ARR | Revenue-based |\n| Account Manager | ¥50M net retention + ¥15M upsell | Revenue-based |\n| Sales Director | Team quota (sum of AEs) | Team revenue |\n| VP Sales | Company new business revenue | Company revenue |\n\n**Quarterly breakdown**: \n- Q1: 20% of annual (ramp-up)\n- Q2: 25% of annual\n- Q3: 25% of annual\n- Q4: 30% of annual (strongest quarter)\n\n### 4.3 Quota Adjustments\n\n**Mid-year adjustments** allowed for:\n- Territory changes\n- Product launches/sunsets\n- Market conditions (e.g., recession)\n- Extended leave (>30 days)\n\n**Process**:\n- Sales rep or manager requests adjustment\n- VP Sales reviews and approves\n- CFO approves if significant (>20% change)\n\n**Not adjusted for**:\n- Individual performance issues\n- Lost deals\n- Competitive pressure (this is normal)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Commission Calculation\n\n### 5.1 For Account Executives (New Business)\n\n**Commission rate**: Tiered based on quota attainment\n\n| Quota Attainment | Commission Rate | Example (¥80M quota) |\n|-----------------|-----------------|----------------------|\n| 0-50% | 5% of ARR | ¥40M closed = ¥2,000K |\n| 51-80% | 7% of ARR | ¥64M closed = ¥4,480K |\n| 81-100% | 10% of ARR | ¥80M closed = ¥8,000K (hits OTE) |\n| 101-125% | 12% of ARR | ¥100M closed = ¥12,000K |\n| 126%+ | 15% of ARR | ¥120M closed = ¥18,000K (accelerator!) |\n\n**Why tiered?**: Reward over-achievement ("accelerators")\n\n**Example calculation** (AE with ¥80M quota):\n- Closes ¥90M (113% of quota)\n- 0-50% tier: ¥40M × 5% = ¥2,000K\n- 51-80%: ¥24M × 7% = ¥1,680K\n- 81-100%: ¥16M × 10% = ¥1,600K\n- 101-113%: ¥10M × 12% = ¥1,200K\n- **Total commission**: ¥6,480K\n\n### 5.2 For SDRs (Lead Generation)\n\n**Commission per SRL** (Sales-Ready Lead):\n\n| SRL Quality | Commission | Criteria |\n|-------------|------------|----------|\n| Accepted SRL | ¥10K | Sales accepts lead within 24 hours |\n| Qualified SRL | ¥15K | Converts to opportunity (BANT qualified) |\n| Closed Deal | ¥50K | SRL results in closed deal (within 6 months) |\n\n**Annual quota**: 120 SRLs\n\n**Example**:\n- 130 SRLs generated (108% of quota)\n- 110 accepted by sales = ¥1,100K\n- 45 qualified = ¥675K\n- 12 closed deals = ¥600K\n- **Total commission**: ¥2,375K (exceeds OTE target of ¥1,500K due to high quality)\n\n### 5.3 For Account Managers (Renewals + Upsell)\n\n**Split compensation**:\n- 60% weighted on net retention\n- 40% weighted on upsell/expansion\n\n**Net retention calculation**:\n- Start: ¥100M ARR book of business\n- Renewals: ¥92M (8% churn)\n- Net retention: 92%\n\n**Commission**:\n- Net retention ≥95%: Full commission (60% of target)\n- Net retention 90-94%: Prorated\n- Net retention <90%: Reduced commission\n\n**Upsell commission**: 8% of net new ARR (upsell/cross-sell)\n\n### 5.4 For Sales Management\n\n**Sales Director**: 70% team quota, 30% individual contribution\n\n**VP Sales**: 100% based on company new business revenue target\n\n**Tiered similar to AE** but lower rates (reflecting less direct sales activity)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Deal Credit and Splits\n\n### 6.1 Standard Credit\n\n**Primary AE**: 100% credit for deals in their territory\n\n**Territory defined by**:\n- Company size\n- Geography\n- Industry vertical (in some cases)\n\n### 6.2 Split Deals\n\n**When deal involves multiple AEs**:\n- Documented agreement before deal closes\n- Typical splits: 50/50 or 60/40 (based on contribution)\n- VP Sales arbitrates disputes\n\n**Example scenarios**:\n- Multi-location deal spanning territories\n- Strategic deal requiring team effort\n- Transfer mid-sales cycle\n\n### 6.3 SDR Credit\n\n**SDR receives lead credit** if:\n- SDR generated the lead\n- Lead converts to opportunity within 30 days\n- AE accepts lead as SRL (Sales-Ready Lead)\n\n**SDR credit timeline**: Up to 6 months from SRL acceptance\n\n### 6.4 Transfers and Reassignments\n\n**If account transferred**:\n- Original AE: Credit for renewals of deals they closed (for 12 months)\n- New AE: Credit for new business and renewals after 12 months\n\n**If AE leaves company**:\n- Open opportunities: Reassigned to another AE (full credit)\n- Closed deals in pipeline: Original AE receives commission (paid out)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Commission Payment\n\n### 7.1 Payment Timing\n\n**80% paid on booking**: When deal is closed and contract signed\n\n**20% paid on cash collection**: When customer payment received (within 45 days)\n\n**Rationale**: Aligns with working capital management (DC_RAJ_005)\n- Incentivizes sales to care about payment terms\n- Reduces bad debt risk\n\n**Example**:\n- Deal closes: ¥10M ARR\n- Commission: ¥1,000K (10% rate)\n- Paid immediately: ¥800K\n- Paid on collection (within 45 days): ¥200K\n\n### 7.2 Payment Schedule\n\n**Monthly commission runs**:\n- Closes through last day of month\n- Commission calculated: 1st-3rd of following month\n- Payment: 15th of following month\n\n**Example**: Deal closes September 25 → Commission paid October 15\n\n### 7.3 New Hire Ramp\n\n**Commission during ramp period**:\n\n| Month | Quota | Commission Rate |\n|-------|-------|----------------|\n| Month 1-2 | 0% (training) | Draw against future (see below) |\n| Month 3 | 50% of full quota | Full commission rate |\n| Month 4-5 | 75% of full quota | Full commission rate |\n| Month 6+ | 100% of full quota | Full commission rate |\n\n**Draw**: Months 1-2, new hire receives guaranteed ¥500K/month (recoverable from future commissions)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Clawbacks and Adjustments\n\n### 8.1 Commission Clawback\n\n**Clawback occurs if**:\n- Customer cancels within 90 days (full clawback)\n- Customer non-payment (proportional clawback)\n- Fraudulent deal (full clawback + termination)\n\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'Sales'});
