252, -0.0017888247, 0.032810945, 0.044443436, 0.05832027, -0.018149648, 0.023234876, 0.0098499125, -0.00048742816, -0.020675778, -0.05204291, -0.0035193753, 0.06452859, -0.047580916, -0.0071616485, 0.009498572, -0.017022707, 0.0664278, 0.043488268, 0.07204882, 0.00478305, 0.028570954, 0.010611165, -0.050515242, -0.00025541647, -0.051943585, 0.05516132, 0.04317991, -0.046162736, -0.043374576, 0.0046329927, -0.016377455, 0.007780359, 0.067609966, -0.023552086, 0.016106468, 0.013128968, -0.002141546, -0.02965826, 0.03820197, 0.015706087, -0.036940124, 0.01672039, -0.0820231, 0.014715864, 0.040502228, 0.0033997062, 0.016651465, -0.018513272, 2.6949243e-34, -0.015205903, -0.046572234, -0.010306194, -0.0041098287, -0.011767648, -0.01809952, 0.017680112, 0.0015815393, -0.011956332, -0.01580055, -0.03824114], embedding_text: 'Policy: Hiring Approval Policy\nVersion: None\nID: POLICY-HR-005\n\nContent:\n# Hiring Approval Policy\n\n**Document ID**: POLICY-HR-005  \n**Version**: 1.2  \n**Effective Date**: February 1, 2024  \n**Owner**: People Operations + CFO Office  \n**Last Updated**: February 1, 2024  \n**Review Frequency**: Annually  \n**Confidentiality**: Internal\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy establishes hiring approval process to ensure:\n- Hiring aligns with business needs and budget\n- Proper cost planning and financial controls\n- Efficient approval workflow\n- Headcount management\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\nApplies to all new hires:\n- Full-time employees\n- Part-time employees\n- Contract/temporary workers (>3 months)\n- Interns\n\nDoes NOT apply to:\n- Replacements for budgeted roles (see Section 4.2)\n- Short-term contractors (<3 months, within budget)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Approval Authority\n\n### 3.1 Approval Thresholds\n\n| Role Level | Annual Comp | Approval Required |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------------|\n| Individual Contributor | <¥10M | Hiring Manager + Department Head |\n| Senior IC / Manager | ¥10M - ¥15M | Department Head + VP + CFO |\n| Director | ¥15M - ¥20M | VP + CFO + CEO |\n| VP / C-Level | >¥20M | CEO + Board Compensation Committee |\n\n**Note**: "Annual Comp" = Base + Target Bonus/Commission + Benefits (~30% loaded)\n\n### 3.2 Headcount Budget\n\n**Annual headcount plan** approved by:\n- Department heads propose\n- CFO reviews financial impact\n- CEO approves\n- Board ratifies in annual budget\n\n**Current year headcount**: Tracked by Finance and HR\n\n**Example FY2024**:\n- Engineering: 55 (currently 45, +10 approved)\n- Sales: 20 (currently 15, +5 approved)\n- Marketing: 25 (currently 22, +3 approved)\n- Product: 26 (currently 22, +4 approved)\n- Customer Success: 22 (currently 18, +4 approved)\n- Finance: 14 (currently 12, +2 approved)\n- People Ops: 10 (currently 8, +2 approved)\n- **Total**: 172 (currently 142, +30 approved for FY2024)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Hiring Request Process\n\n### 4.1 New Position (Not in Budget)\n\n**Process**:\n1. **Business case required** (template in HR system)\n   - Why is role needed?\n   - What business impact?\n   - What happens if we don\'t hire?\n   - ROI calculation (if applicable)\n   - Budget impact\n\n2. **Department head approval**\n   - Validates business need\n   - Confirms priority vs. other roles\n   - Allocates from department budget\n\n3. **CFO review**\n   - Financial impact assessment\n   - Headcount budget impact\n   - Compensation benchmarking\n   - Approves if justified\n\n4. **CEO approval** (if >¥15M or strategic)\n   - Strategic alignment\n   - Company priorities\n   - Final decision\n\n**Timeline**: 5-10 business days\n\n**Context**: See DC_RAJ_001 for precedent (Sales team expansion request)\n\n### 4.2 Replacement Hire (Budgeted)\n\n**Process** (simplified):\n1. **Hiring manager submits** replacement request\n2. **HR verifies** position was budgeted\n3. **Department head approves** (no CFO needed if like-for-like)\n4. **Post immediately**\n\n**Timeline**: 1-2 business days\n\n**Definition**: "Like-for-like" = same level, same compensation range\n\n**If upgrade**: Treat as new position (requires CFO approval)\n\n### 4.3 Backfill After Departure\n\n**Automatic approval** if:\n- Departure occurred <90 days ago\n- Position was budgeted\n- Hiring at same or lower level\n\n**Delayed backfill** (>90 days):\n- Re-justify business need\n- Market may have changed\n- Department head approval required\n\n**Not automatic**: Company may decide not to backfill (re-org, changed priorities)\n\n### 4.4 Emergency Hiring\n\n**Definition**: Critical business need requiring urgent hire\n- Key customer escalation\n- System outage requiring specialized skill\n- Legal/compliance requirement\n\n**Process**:\n- Verbal approval from VP + CFO\n- Written justification within 24 hours\n- Retroactive formal approval\n\n**Limit**: 2 emergency hires per department per year\n\n---\n\n## 5. Job Description and Leveling\n\n### 5.1 Job Description Required\n\n**Before posting, JD must include**:\n- Role title and level\n- Department and reporting structure\n- Key responsibilities (5-8 bullets)\n- Required qualifications\n- Preferred qualifications\n- Compensation range\n- Location (office/remote)\n\n**Template**: Available in HR system\n\n**Review**: HR reviews for:\n- Appropriate leveling\n- Competitive requirements\n- Legal compliance (no discriminatory language)\n- Inclusive language\n\n### 5.2 Leveling Standards\n\n**Engineering example**:\n- Junior Engineer (Level 1): ¥5M - ¥7M\n- Engineer (Level 2): ¥7M - ¥10M\n- Senior Engineer (Level 3): ¥10M - ¥14M\n- Staff Engineer (Level 4): ¥14M - ¥18M\n- Principal Engineer (Level 5): ¥18M - ¥24M\n\n**Leveling guidelines**: See Career Frameworks (Professional Development Policy)\n\n**Consistency**: HR ensures equivalent levels across departments\n\n---\n\n## 6. Compensation Approval\n\n### 6.1 Compensation Bands\n\n**Each role has defined band**:\n- Minimum: Entry-level for that role\n- Midpoint: Experienced performer\n- Maximum: Expert/top performer\n\n**Example - Senior Engineer**:\n- Min: ¥10M\n- Mid: ¥12M\n- Max: ¥14M\n\n**New hire typically**: 10th-50th percentile (room for growth)\n\n### 6.2 Exceeding Band\n\n**If candidate requires above-band compensation**:\n- Justify in writing (unique skills, competitive offer, market conditions)\n- CFO approval required\n- Consider: Level up instead (if qualifications match)\n\n**Red flag**: Consistently hiring above band indicates band needs adjustment\n\n### 6.3 Equity/Stock Options\n\n**For employees eligible for equity**:\n- Grant size based on level and role\n- Approved by CEO\n- Board approval for VP+ grants\n- Subject to equity plan limits\n\n**Current practice**: Directors and above receive equity\n\n---\n\n## 7. Budget Impact Assessment\n\n### 7.1 Fully Loaded Cost\n\n**CFO calculates**:\n- Base salary\n- Bonuses/commission (target)\n- Benefits (~30% of base in Japan)\n  - Health insurance\n  - Pension\n  - Unemployment insurance\n  - Other statutory benefits\n- Equipment and onboarding (~¥500K one-time)\n- Workspace costs (if office-based)\n\n**Example**:\n- Senior Engineer base: ¥12M\n- Benefits: ¥3.6M (30%)\n- Equipment: ¥500K (one-time)\n- **Total Year 1**: ¥16.1M\n- **Ongoing annual**: ¥15.6M\n\n### 7.2 Budget Allocation\n\n**Hiring reduces available budget**:\n- Department budget: ¥450M for Engineering\n- Hire Senior Engineer: ¥15.6M annual\n- Remaining budget: ¥434.4M\n\n**Tracking**: Finance tracks in real-time dashboard\n\n### 7.3 Budget Overruns\n\n**If department exceeds budget**:\n- Must justify to CFO\n- May require offsetting (defer other hire, reduce spend elsewhere)\n- CEO approval for >10% overage\n\n---\n\n## 8. Hiring Timeline\n\n### 8.1 Standard Timeline\n\n**Typical timeline** (from approval to start):\n\n| Phase | Duration | Responsible |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| Job posting preparation | 3-5 days | Hiring Manager + HR |\n| Active sourcing | 2-4 weeks | Recruiter + Hiring Manager |\n| Interviews | 2-3 weeks | Interview panel |\n| Reference checks | 3-5 days | HR |\n| Offer preparation | 2-3 days | HR + CFO (if needed) |\n| Candidate decision | 3-7 days | Candidate |\n| Notice period | 4-8 weeks (Japan standard) | Candidate |\n| **Total** | **10-16 weeks** | |\n\n**Expedited hiring**: Possible for critical roles (with VP approval)\n\n### 8.2 Time to Fill Targets\n\n**By role type**:\n- Junior roles: 6-8 weeks\n- Mid-level roles: 8-12 weeks\n- Senior roles: 12-16 weeks\n- Executive roles: 16-24 weeks\n\n**Measured**: Time from approval to start date\n\n---\n\n## 9. Internal vs. External Hiring\n\n### 9.1 Internal Candidates First\n\n**Policy**: Post internally for 5 days before external posting\n\n**Benefits**:\n- Lower cost (no recruiter fees)\n- Faster onboarding\n- Known performer\n- Employee development and retention\n\n**Process**: Internal candidates apply via HR system\n\n### 9.2 Internal Hiring Approval\n\n**Simplified process**:\n- Hiring manager approval\n- Current manager notified (transparency)\n- HR facilitates transition\n- 4-week transition period (typically)\n\n**Budget**: No additional headcount (transfer)\n\n---\n\n## 10. Contractor and Temporary Workers\n\n### 10.1 When to Use Contractors\n\n**Appropriate for**:\n- Short-term projects (<6 months)\n- Speci\n\n[Content truncated due to length...]', category: 'People'});
